  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The Rosenmund reaction is a hydrogenation process where molecular hydrogen reacts with the acyl chloride in the presence of a catalyst – palladium on barium sulphate. Barium sulphate reduces the activity of palladium due to its low surface area, thereby preventing over reduction.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/4cd92292-cd2e-4a01-b2bc-91f7ec1d36ef.png\" style=\"width: 550px; height: 161px;\"/></p><p>It is known as rosenmund reduction, which is the partial reduction of acid chloride to aldehyde.</p><p>Hence, the answer is option A.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
